<title>FRANCE: Bouygues gets 100 mln Ffr German contract.</title>
<headline>Bouygues gets 100 mln Ffr German contract.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-12-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>French building group Bouygues said on Tuesday it was part of a consortium that had obtained a 500 million franc contract to build a subway line in Dusseldorf.</p>
<p>Bouygues said in a statement its share of the contract was 100 million francs. Four German firms also belong to the consortium. Work on the line is set to begin in January and last for five years, with the opening scheduled for the year 2001.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom, +33 1 4221 5452</p>
</text>
